solreign-mystery-s07-directive-scrap =
    MEMO FROM COMPLIANCE — INTERNAL SCHEDULING ONLY, DO NOT POST

    A reminder to whoever inherits this desk: the Directive
    rotation is fixed, not drawn. Twelve slots, same order, every
    cycle, no exceptions. Consult the master calendar, not the
    rumor mill, if anyone asks.

    Slot seven is the rotation's one exception to "no exceptions."
    Its posted text reads as generic Surveillance Sweep language.
    Its actual content, per the calendar's own footnote, is a
    single standing instruction: "Berth 07 is not to be reassigned
    on this rotation, or any other."

    Nobody currently in Compliance wrote that footnote. Nobody in
    Compliance has removed it, either.

solreign-mystery-s07-policy-addendum =
    SOLREIGN HR POLICY MANUAL — ADDENDUM 7-C
    (Stamped: NOT FOR FILING WITH EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK. Separate volume.)

    RE: Subject-Class Designations

    A "Subject" designation is a liability classification, not a
    legal identity. It marks an asset, a berth, or a liquidation-
    queue slot currently under active review. Personnel may be
    temporarily bound to a Subject designation for the duration of
    that review.

    The designation persists after the personnel do not. This is
    intentional. Continuity of paperwork outranks continuity of
    staff.

    STATUS OF SUBJECT 07: [stamp smudged — reads BOUND or UNBOUND
    depending on the angle of the light]

